  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEETUG_BIOLOGY_REPRODUCTIONINORGANISMS_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Asexual reproductive structures in Penicillium</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The given schematic diagram represents an asexual reproductive structure commonly observed in a member of Kingdom Fungi. Identify the structure labelled <strong>X</strong> and the organism in which it is found.</p>
<div style="margin:12px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 260" width="320" height="260" role="img" aria-label="Schematic diagram of asexual reproductive structures in a fungus">
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="320" height="260" fill="#ffffff"/>
    <!-- Main stalk (conidiophore) -->
    <path d="M145,235 L145,150 Q145,135 130,120 L115,100" fill="none" stroke="#3b5e2b" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <path d="M145,150 Q145,135 160,120 L175,100" fill="none" stroke="#3b5e2b" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <path d="M145,145 L145,98" fill="none" stroke="#3b5e2b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <!-- Sterigmata / Phialides -->
    <ellipse cx="112" cy="92" rx="5" ry="10" fill="#7aa352" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5" transform="rotate(-20 112 92)"/>
    <ellipse cx="145" cy="90" rx="5" ry="10" fill="#7aa352" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <ellipse cx="178" cy="92" rx="5" ry="10" fill="#7aa352" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5" transform="rotate(20 178 92)"/>
    <!-- Chains of conidia -->
    <!-- Left chain -->
    <circle cx="106" cy="76" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="101" cy="62" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="96" cy="48" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="91" cy="34" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Middle chain -->
    <circle cx="145" cy="74" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="145" cy="59" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="145" cy="44" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="145" cy="29" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Right chain -->
    <circle cx="184" cy="76" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="189" cy="62" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="194" cy="48" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="199" cy="34" r="6" fill="#9bc56d" stroke="#2d4720" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Pointer line and label X -->
    <line x1="206" y1="34" x2="255" y2="34" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <line x1="201" y1="48" x2="255" y2="34" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <text x="262" y="39" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111111">X</text>
  </svg>
</div>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>The schematic shows an upright, branched stalk bearing flask-shaped cells at its tips, from which chains of rounded, non-motile asexual spores (labelled X) are produced exogenously in succession.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>Members of Kingdom Fungi and simple plants such as algae reproduce through special asexual reproductive structures. In <em>Penicillium</em>, asexual reproduction takes place by non-motile spores called conidia, which are borne in chains on branched conidiophores.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Comparison with Other Structures</strong><br/>Zoospores are microscopic motile flagellated structures found in algae like <em>Chlamydomonas</em>. Buds are small outgrowths formed in organisms like yeast and <em>Hydra</em>, while gemmules are internal asexual reproductive structures found in sponges.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The structure labelled X represents conidia, and the organism shown is <em>Penicillium</em>.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Zoospores; <em>Chlamydomonas</em></p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Conidia; <em>Penicillium</em></p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Gemmules; Sponge</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Buds; <em>Hydra</em></p>]]></text></answer>
