  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEETUG_BIOLOGY_REPRODUCTIONINORGANISMS_DIAGRAM_Q02 - Sex organs and sexuality in Chara</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The given schematic diagram illustrates the reproductive structures located at a node of <em>Chara</em>. Identify the structures labelled <strong>P</strong> and <strong>Q</strong>, and choose the correct description of the organism's sexuality.</p>
<div style="margin:12px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 340 260" width="340" height="260" role="img" aria-label="Schematic diagram of reproductive organs in Chara">
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="340" height="260" fill="#ffffff"/>
    <!-- Main stem axis -->
    <rect x="75" y="20" width="16" height="220" fill="#b7d97e" stroke="#355e1b" stroke-width="2"/>
    <line x1="80" y1="20" x2="80" y2="240" stroke="#5b8c32" stroke-width="1"/>
    <line x1="86" y1="20" x2="86" y2="240" stroke="#5b8c32" stroke-width="1"/>
    <!-- Lateral branchlets -->
    <polygon points="91,150 155,75 162,82 91,165" fill="#cbe599" stroke="#355e1b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <polygon points="91,158 170,115 174,123 91,170" fill="#cbe599" stroke="#355e1b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Upper female sex organ (Oogonium) -->
    <ellipse cx="122" cy="95" rx="18" ry="30" fill="#b5673b" stroke="#4a2611" stroke-width="2" transform="rotate(20 122 95)"/>
    <!-- Spiral lines on oogonium -->
    <path d="M110,80 Q125,85 136,78" fill="none" stroke="#4a2611" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <path d="M106,92 Q122,98 138,90" fill="none" stroke="#4a2611" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <path d="M105,105 Q120,110 135,102" fill="none" stroke="#4a2611" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <!-- Corona at apex of oogonium -->
    <path d="M126,65 L122,55 L130,58 L135,52 L138,60 L144,57 L140,67 Z" fill="#e6d67a" stroke="#4a2611" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <!-- Lower male sex organ (Antheridium) -->
    <circle cx="136" cy="158" r="24" fill="#d97592" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="2"/>
    <circle cx="136" cy="158" r="18" fill="#f2e69b" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    <line x1="136" y1="140" x2="136" y2="176" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="1"/>
    <line x1="118" y1="158" x2="154" y2="158" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="1"/>
    <line x1="123" y1="145" x2="149" y2="171" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="1"/>
    <line x1="149" y1="145" x2="123" y2="171" stroke="#5e1d30" stroke-width="1"/>
    <!-- Labels P and Q -->
    <line x1="141" y1="92" x2="215" y2="92" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <text x="222" y="97" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111111">P</text>
    <line x1="160" y1="158" x2="215" y2="158" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <text x="222" y="163" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111111">Q</text>
  </svg>
</div>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>The diagram shows a node of the green alga <em>Chara</em> bearing two distinct reproductive structures on the same plant axis. The elongated, spirally striated structure positioned above (labelled P) is the female sex organ, and the spherical structure positioned below it (labelled Q) is the male sex organ.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>In plants and algae, organisms that possess both male and female reproductive structures on the same individual are termed bisexual, homothallic, or monoecious. Conversely, organisms in which male and female sex organs are borne on separate individuals are termed unisexual, heterothallic, or dioecious.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Identification of Structures and Sexuality</strong><br/>In <em>Chara</em>, the upper female sex organ is the oogonium (nucule), and the lower male sex organ is the antheridium (globule). Because both the oogonium and the antheridium are present on the same plant body, <em>Chara</em> is a monoecious (bisexual) plant.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>Structure P is the oogonium, structure Q is the antheridium, and <em>Chara</em> is a monoecious plant.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P is antheridium, Q is oogonium; <em>Chara</em> is dioecious</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P is oogonium, Q is antheridium; <em>Chara</em> is dioecious</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P is oogonium, Q is antheridium; <em>Chara</em> is monoecious</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P is archegoniophore, Q is antheridiophore; <em>Chara</em> is monoecious</p>]]></text></answer>
