  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEETUG_BIOLOGY_REPRODUCTIONINORGANISMS_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Vegetative propagule in Bryophyllum leaf</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Observe the given schematic diagram of a vegetative propagule in <em>Bryophyllum</em>. Which of the following accurately identifies the structures labelled <strong>X</strong>, their site of origin, and the genetic nature of the resulting plantlets?</p>
<div style="margin:12px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 340 270" width="340" height="270" role="img" aria-label="Schematic diagram of vegetative propagation in Bryophyllum leaf">
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="340" height="270" fill="#ffffff"/>
    <!-- Leaf blade with notched margin -->
    <path d="M135,235 Q95,215 80,180 Q70,155 82,135 Q72,115 88,92 Q86,68 112,55 Q135,40 160,55 Q188,65 194,95 Q208,118 196,145 Q205,172 185,198 Q168,222 145,235 Z" fill="#c7e68b" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="2"/>
    <!-- Petiole and midrib -->
    <path d="M140,255 L140,235 L138,60" fill="none" stroke="#4d7a28" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <!-- Lateral veins -->
    <path d="M139,190 L95,165 M139,155 L92,130 M139,120 L98,95 M139,88 L115,65" fill="none" stroke="#4d7a28" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <path d="M139,190 L180,168 M139,155 L188,135 M139,120 L185,98 M139,88 L165,68" fill="none" stroke="#4d7a28" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Adventitious plantlet 1 (top left notch) -->
    <g transform="translate(88, 92)">
      <path d="M0,0 L-12,-22" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="2"/>
      <ellipse cx="-18" cy="-28" rx="8" ry="4" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(-30 -18 -28)"/>
      <ellipse cx="-6" cy="-30" rx="8" ry="4" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(30 -6 -30)"/>
      <path d="M0,0 L-6,10 M0,0 L0,12 M0,0 L5,9" stroke="#5e4326" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    </g>
    <!-- Adventitious plantlet 2 (right notch) -->
    <g transform="translate(194, 118)">
      <path d="M0,0 L16,-18" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="2"/>
      <ellipse cx="22" cy="-24" rx="8" ry="4" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(-35 22 -24)"/>
      <ellipse cx="10" cy="-24" rx="8" ry="4" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(35 10 -24)"/>
      <path d="M0,0 L-4,10 M0,0 L2,12 M0,0 L7,9" stroke="#5e4326" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    </g>
    <!-- Adventitious plantlet 3 (bottom left notch) -->
    <g transform="translate(80, 180)">
      <path d="M0,0 L-16,-14" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="2"/>
      <ellipse cx="-22" cy="-18" rx="7" ry="3.5" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(-25 -22 -18)"/>
      <ellipse cx="-10" cy="-20" rx="7" ry="3.5" fill="#89bd46" stroke="#365c1b" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(25 -10 -20)"/>
      <path d="M0,0 L-5,10 M0,0 L1,11" stroke="#5e4326" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    </g>
    <!-- Label X -->
    <line x1="216" y1="94" x2="265" y2="70" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <line x1="100" y1="62" x2="265" y2="70" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <text x="272" y="75" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111111">X</text>
  </svg>
</div>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>The diagram shows a leaf of <em>Bryophyllum</em> with small plantlets bearing tiny leaves and roots (labelled X) emerging along the notched outer margins of the leaf blade.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>Vegetative propagation in plants is a mode of asexual reproduction because new offspring are produced from a single parent without the involvement of gamete formation or fusion. Consequently, the offspring formed are morphologically and genetically identical to the parent and are referred to as clones.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Site of Origin in <em>Bryophyllum</em></strong><br/>Unlike potato tubers or ginger rhizomes where new plantlets arise from buds at the nodes of modified stems, in <em>Bryophyllum</em>, adventitious buds arise from the notches present at the margins of the leaves. When these buds develop into plantlets and come in contact with damp soil, they grow into independent plants that are genetically identical clones of the parent.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The structures labelled X are adventitious buds arising from notches at the leaf margins, and the resulting plantlets are clones of the parent plant.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Axillary buds arising from stem nodes; the resulting plantlets are genetically diverse.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Adventitious buds arising from the midrib; the resulting plantlets are haploid.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Gemmules arising from the leaf petiole; the resulting plantlets are genetically identical to the parent.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Adventitious buds arising from notches at leaf margins; the resulting plantlets are clones of the parent.</p>]]></text></answer>
